  "event_seq": 276,
  "root_problem": "Since August 2026, CRM dispute-ticket volume roughly doubled (610→1260/month, E-03). The dominant confirmed mechanism: billing import rule BV-17 (deployed 2026-08-01) compares raw AMI register values to 12-month m3 history with unit_scaling 'none' (E-14), while firmware v4.2 meters (rolled out 2026-06) report in 0.1 m3 units (E-13); valid v4.2 reads therefore appear ~10x inflated and are rejected REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION, forcing estimate substitution that accounts for 1184 of 1240 disputed ESTIMATED bills (95.5%, E-12). This is a billing-config defect, not an AMI/MDMS pipeline failure (H-AMI-MDMS-PIPELINE-FAILURE rejected by E-14) nor field staffing/route lateness (rejected by E-12). The mechanism behind the separate majority of disputed bills carrying an ACTUAL read type (1785 of 3025, E-04) remains unestablished by current evidence."
 },
